<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Riyadh Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2019</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemeni-civil-war-2014-present">Yemeni civil war (2014–present)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> Agreement was signed on 5 November 2019 between the internationally recognised Yemeni government and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-transitional-council">Southern Transitional Council</a> under Saudi mediation, after the council's forces had seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> in August. It provided for a power-sharing government and the integration of southern forces into the army and police. Implementation was slow and incomplete, and tensions between the two sides continued.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/riyadh-agreement.jpg" alt="Riyadh Agreement" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saudi Press Agency · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Signing_ceremony_of_the_Riyadh_agreement.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
